All rights reserved.

## 1. Definitions

"Software" refers to the FelixGPT project, including its source code, scripts, model architectures, documentation and associated original materials.

"Author" refers to the original creator of FelixGPT.

"Derivative Works" refers to modified versions, adaptations or extensions of the Software.

## 2. Permissions

The Author grants permission to individuals to:

- View and study the source code.
- Use the Software for personal and educational purposes.
- Modify and experiment with the Software.
- Create Derivative Works.
- Share and redistribute the original or modified Software, subject to the conditions below.

## 3. Attribution Requirements

Any redistribution or publication of the Software or Derivative Works must:

- Clearly acknowledge FelixGPT as the original project.
- Credit the original Author.
- Retain this licence and all original copyright notices.
- Clearly identify significant modifications made by other contributors.
- Not falsely claim original authorship of the original FelixGPT work.

Suggested attribution:

"Based on FelixGPT, originally developed by Felix Paulin."

## 4. Redistribution

Redistribution of the Software and Derivative Works is permitted for non-commercial purposes, provided all attribution requirements in Section 3 are met.

Redistributors must include a copy of this licence with their distribution.

## 5. Commercial Use

Commercial use, commercial redistribution, or incorporation of the Software into commercial products or services requires prior written permission from the Author.

## 6. Restrictions

Users may not:

- Remove or alter original copyright notices.
- Misrepresent the original authorship of FelixGPT.
- Redistribute the Software without complying with this licence.
- Claim ownership of the original FelixGPT source code or original contributions.

## 7. Ownership

The original Software and its original contributions remain the intellectual property of the Author.

Permission to use or modify the Software does not transfer ownership of the original work.

Contributions made by other individuals remain subject to their respective ownership rights.

## 8. Disclaimer of Warranty

The Software is provided "AS IS", without warranty of any kind, express or implied.

The Author shall not be held liable for claims, damages or other liabilities arising from the use or distribution of the Software, to the extent permitted by applicable law.

## 9. Termination

Permissions granted under this licence terminate automatically if a user materially violates its conditions.

